<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <PackageId>DeepSharp.Pipelines</PackageId>
    <Description>Pipeline-driven design for .NET: declare the whole course from raw data to a validated model once, as one artefact, and replay it. The chain is the enforcement — anything that learns from the data is only offered after you have said how to split, so fitting on everything is not a mistake you can make and be warned about later. A declaration written in C# and one written as a file reach equally far, and each is the other read back. Each column's kind is proposed from what every cell says, for a person to accept or change; a profile names what should not be there; a learner says what it needs where the features are handed over — every feature declared to land between minus one and one, numbers left on their own scale, or categories as places — and a run for it leaves out the steps it has no use for; and a report, declared with the pipeline before any number exists, measures a trained model in the answer's own units, each measure beside what predicting the training rows' average scores.</Description>
    <PackageTags>machine-learning;pipeline;data-preparation;feature-engineering;normalization;data-leakage;etl;dataframe;dotnet</PackageTags>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Abstractions only: a pipeline can be registered in a host that has a container, and built with
         `new` in a program that has none. The library never requires one. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="10.*" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- A file's own text is escaped for a refusal by one internal rule, reached directly by its tests as the core
         library's own is. -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="DeepSharp.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\assets\icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
